<br/>When fully raid buffed with consumables, a bear wearing the above set will achieve the following tank metrics:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">54,528 HP (<i>far</i> more than any other tank spec)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">33,643 armor</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">58.6% avoidance</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">10,100 TPS</div></li></ul>The ability to access such a sky-high effective health pool (EHP) while wearing primarily melee DPS gear makes Feral Druids phenomenal off-tanks in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a>, particularly on encounters like <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=33515/auriaya">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Auriaya</span></a> or Hard Mode <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=33271/general-vezax">
<span class="tinyicontxt">General Vezax</span></a> where the off-tank may spend a significant fraction of the encounter DPSing in their tank gear.<br/>
<br/>Note that the displayed configuration is optimized for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> players. If you are an <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> bear and are lucky enough to have a <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/draenei">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Draenei</span></a> in your party providing the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> buff, then the only required change is to swap out the single <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40088/vivid-forest-emerald">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_25.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vivid Forest Emerald</span></a> gem that is used for a <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40091/forceful-forest-emerald">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_25.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Forceful Forest Emerald</span></a> instead, since the Hit Rating on the former will be wasted due to the reduced cap of 7%.<br/>
<br/>While the above gear set is capable of surviving all of the raid content in Phase 2, a select few boss encounters, most notably Hard Mode <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32867/steelbreaker">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Steelbreaker</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a>, are known to be particularly punishing on tanks even when the content is on farm. For this reason, a second "maximum survival" gear set is presented below, with the goal of minimizing the risk of a tank death on these few encounters:<br/>
