<br/>Compared to the balanced configuration, the pure survival setup above swaps in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45485/bronze-pendant-of-the-vanir">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_47.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bronze Pendant of the Vanir</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45112/the-leviathans-coil">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_71.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Leviathan's Coil</span></a>, and three additional pieces of Season 6 PvP gear in order to access even higher Stamina and avoidance levels.<br/>
<br/>Note that both of the above BiS setups include the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=63770/reticulated-armor-webbing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reticulated Armor Webbing</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67839/mind-amplification-dish">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mind Amplification Dish</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that it is assumed that any competitive Feral tank player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Conquest for Feral Druid Tank Phase 2</h3>There are no <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=221/emblem-of-conquest">
